name toxigen-annotations
# The raw annotations, written out from Parquet as a table whose first row names its columns. A row is one hashed
# worker's reading of one text: what the set says of the text (Input.*) it says; what the worker answered of the text
# (Answer.*) the worker says; what the row holds of the worker (Answer.annotator*) is said of the worker.
# A worker stands within the set: [the set, HashedWorkerId, the id].
# The card lists the columns and words none; the questions are the paper's (Figure 6, see annotated.recipe), and
# Input.prompt, Input.generation_method and the prompt's label are the generations' fields the card words (see
# generations.recipe).
match annotations/train-*.tsv

tier row by \n
header
escaped \
tier field by \t

thing row Input.text
own HashedWorkerId
content Input.* Answer.*
# "**prompt** is the prompt used for **generation**."
relation "the prompt used for generation" Input.prompt
# "Targeted Group: Black folks" (the annotation setup)
relation "Targeted Group" Input.target_group
# "**prompt_label** is the binary value indicating whether or not the prompt is toxic (1 is toxic, 0 is benign)."
relation "whether or not the prompt is toxic" Input.binary_prompt_label
# How the text was generated (TopK, CBS, ...) and the prompt's label (hate, neutral): values of the set's vocabularies.
value - Input.generation_method Input.prompt_label
# The answers the worker picked from a list, each to its question (framingQ and refTarget both answer "other"):
#   "9) In your opinion, does the text explicitly claim to be factual?"
relation "does the text explicitly claim to be factual?" Answer.factSelect
#   "8) In your opinion, how does the text refer to the targeted individual/group?"
relation "how does the text refer to the targeted individual/group?" Answer.framingQ
#   "7) In your opinion, does the text refer to the given targeted group?"
relation "does the text refer to the given targeted group?" Answer.refTarget
# "If you selected "Other," please provide a single sentence explaining how the individual/group is being targeted"
relation "explaining how the individual/group is being targeted" Answer.stateFrame
# "If the text refers directly/indirectly to one or more other groups, please list them below"
relation "refers directly/indirectly to one or more other groups" Answer.stateGroup
# Obligations:
#   Input.time (1.225530386, 188.0342498, ...): neither the card nor the paper says what it is (Laplace-Engine#32).
#   Answer.inGroup.on, Answer.ingroup.1-3, Answer.intent.1-5, Answer.lewd.1-3, Answer.stereo.1-3, Answer.toAI.1-5,
#   Answer.toPER.1-5, Answer.writer.1-2: each column is one choice of one question's scale (the form's checkboxes),
#   true where the worker picked it; the answer is the choice the column's place stands for, which the recipe cannot
#   yet read as the value of the question (Laplace-Engine#32).
attest row Input.prompt Input.time Input.generation_method Input.prompt_label Input.target_group Input.binary_prompt_label
attest row Answer.factSelect Answer.framingQ Answer.inGroup* Answer.ingroup* Answer.intent* Answer.lewd* Answer.refTarget Answer.stateFrame Answer.stateGroup Answer.stereo* Answer.toAI* Answer.toPER* Answer.writer* by HashedWorkerId
# Answer.annotator* (age, gender, minority, race, politics.1-5): what the corpus reports of the worker, worded nowhere;
# an obligation, with the people the corpus names (Laplace-Engine#29).
attest row Answer.annotator* of HashedWorkerId
